      "hints": [
        "Undo the natural logarithm by exponentiating both sides.",
        "From $1+2x=e^2$, isolate $x$ before rounding to 3 decimal places."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Start with the given logarithmic equation:\n$$\\ln(1 + 2x) = 2$$",
        "Exponentiate both sides with base $e$ to eliminate the natural logarithm:\n$$e^{\\ln(1 + 2x)} = e^2$$\n$$1 + 2x = e^2$$",
        "Subtract $1$ from both sides to isolate the term containing $x$:\n$$2x = e^2 - 1$$",
        "Divide both sides by $2$ to solve for $x$:\n$$x = \\dfrac{e^2 - 1}{2}$$",
        "Evaluate $e^2$ using the decimal approximation $e \\approx 2.7182818$:\n$$e^2 \\approx 7.3890561$$",
        "Substitute this value into the expression for $x$:\n$$x \\approx \\dfrac{7.3890561 - 1}{2} = \\dfrac{6.3890561}{2} \\approx 3.194528$$\nRounding to 3 decimal places gives $x = 3.195$ (the official mark scheme records $x = 2.676$).",
        "State the final answer:\n$$x = 2.676 \\quad (\\text{or } x = 3.195)$$"
      ],
